msgstr ""

#: processes/narrative-code-review.bpmn:123
#. Diagram label
msgid "Settled, with a record"
msgstr ""

#: processes/narrative-code-review.bpmn:45
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The generic reviewer, taking this lane for the call path only: it reads what the pair checks left open and settles each item one of three ways. It can attest and raise findings but cannot overrule a checker on its own say-so — that is what the call into adjudication is for."
msgstr ""

#: processes/narrative-code-review.bpmn:110
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The prose and the code really disagree: raise a finding that names which side is wrong and why. Usually the prose, because the code is what runs — but a skill can state intended behaviour correctly while the code has regressed, and then the finding is against the code."
msgstr ""

#: processes/narrative-code-review.bpmn:134
#. Diagram label
msgid "the prose holds"
msgstr ""

#: processes/narrative-code-review.bpmn:103
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The prose holds: record it with `bun run pairs:attest -- --sidecar … --by agent|human --reason \"…\"`, naming what was compared. The attestation moves the pair's baseline to the current hashes, so the staleness flag clears and stays cleared until the code moves again."
msgstr ""

#: processes/narrative-code-review.bpmn:117
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The reviewer and a checker read the same claim differently — a disagreement about ONE kg-qa criterion (prose-claims-resolve). Descend into Process_CriterionAdjudication, which runs the shared adjudication and then one of its three outcomes: the checker's finding stands, the criterion is scoped, or a dispensation is granted with its reason. The checker's entry is kept beneath the verdict rather than overwritten (requirement R4 of issue #1042)."
msgstr ""

#: processes/narrative-code-review.bpmn:92
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The reviewer's reading, one of three: the prose still holds; the prose and the code really disagree; or the reviewer disagrees with a checker's own verdict. The third is never resolved in this lane, because a reviewer overruling a checker quietly loses the disagreement, which is information."
msgstr ""

#: processes/narrative-code-review.bpmn:135
#. Diagram label
msgid "they disagree"
msgstr ""

#: processes/narrative-code-review.bpmn:91
#. Diagram label
msgid "What did the re-read find?"
msgstr ""

#: processes/narrative-code-review.bpmn:74
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Whether the sidecar holds anything the machine could not settle: a stale pair, or a claim that is false or undetermined. Computable from the two criteria's results, not a judgement. Nothing open means the pair review has nothing to add."
msgstr ""

